<title>POLAND: Poland offers PLN 200 mln of fixed bonds on Mar 20.</title>
<headline>Poland offers PLN 200 mln of fixed bonds on Mar 20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will offer 200 million zlotys of fixed five-year 12 percent bonds at a tender on March 20, 1997, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>It said the value date for the bonds, due June 12, 2001, will be April 5, 1997.</p>
<p>The bonds on offer come from an earlier three billion zloty issue of 12-percent five-year bonds.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
